==History==
2019
*The Fisherman was once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Fisherman Draft Challenge]], which started on 4/7/2019. In this [[Tournament|challenge]], gameplay was similar to a regular Draft Challenge, except that one of the players was able to choose who would use the Fisherman. If the player achieved at least 9 wins, they obtained the Fisherman early.
*From 28/7/2019 through 30/7/2019, the [[Shop]] had a special offer where [[Arenas|Arena]] 10+ players could buy up to 2 special Fortune [[Chests]] for 500 [[Gems]] that guarantee a Fisherman.
*The Fisherman [[Cards|card]] was generally released on 5/8/2019. On the same day, a [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (5/8/2019)|Balance Update]], increased the Fisherman's hitpoints by 10% and his hook range to 7 tiles (from 6.5 tiles).
*On 2/9/2019, a [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (2/9/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Fisherman's cost to 3 [[Elixir]] (from 4 Elixir) and decreased his damage by 11%.
*On 5/9/2019, a [[Version History#Maintenance%20Break%20(5/9/2019)|maintenance break]], decreased the Fisherman's hitpoints by 5%.
*On 7/10/2019, a [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (7/10/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Fisherman's hitpoints by 5% and his damage by 6%.
*On 4/11/2019, a [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (4/11/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Fisherman's hook range to 6 tiles (from 7 tiles) and increased his hook charge time to 1.1 seconds (from 1 second).
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], added a card render to the Fisherman's card info screen.
2020 
*On 2/1/2020, a maintenence break, fixed an issue where the Fisherman's [[Star Points|Star Level]] used the sound effects of the [[Musketeer]].
*On 7/1/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (7/1/2020)|Balance Update]], increased the Fisherman's hook range to 7 tiles (from 6 tiles) and increased his hook charge time to 1.5 seconds (from 1.1 seconds).
*On 7/7/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (7/7/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the Fisherman's hook charge time to 1.3 seconds (from 1.5 seconds), decreased his attack time interval to 1.3 seconds (from 1.5 seconds), and decreased his first attack time interval to 0.1 seconds (from 0.3 seconds).
*On 9/12/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (9/12/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the Fisherman's hitpoints by 10%.
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Fisherman from Hog Mountain to Legendary Arena. It also fixed some issues with the Fisherman.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022
*On 30/3/2022, the [[Version History#Miner%20Update%20(30/3/2022)|Miner Update]], fixed an issue where Fisherman would become stuck after his target dies during [[Basics of Battle|battle]].
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Fisherman from Legendary Arena to Miner's Mine. It also fixed a bug where [[Sparky]] was not reset when hit by [[Electro Spirit]] at the same time she was being hooked by Fisherman.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2025
*On 8/1/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/1/2025)|Balance Update]], decreased the Fisherman's slow duration to 1.5 seconds (from 2.5 seconds).
*On 31/3/2024, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], decreased the Fisherman's hitpoints by 0.11% and increased his damage by 0.51%.
*On 6/10/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/10/2025)=|Balance Update]] decreased the slowdown effect to -30% (from -35%).
2026

* On 6/4/2026, a Balance Update, removed the FIsherman's slowdown effect entirely

