==Trivia== 
*Archaeological evidence suggests that fishing was invented in East Asia 40,000 years ago, shown from isotopic analysis of the skeletal remains of Tianyuan man that he regularly consumed freshwater fish. Initially, it was done with spearfishing with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harpoon harpoons], but later at around 8,000 years ago, newer methods were developed which are still used to this day.
**In the Korean language setting of the game, the Fisherman's name translates to "Angler".
*In the French language setting of the game, the species of the fish the Fisherman holds is revealed to be a ''Dicentrarchus labrax'' ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_bass European bass]).
*The Fisherman is tied with [[Valkyrie]] for the highest first attack speed of all troops, with a first attack speed of 0.1 seconds.
*The Fisherman is one of the first troop [[cards]] to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], Valkyrie, [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], and [[Night Witch]].
*The Fisherman have been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Fisherman is 1 of 3 troops that has been featured in the [[Treasure Hunt|Capture the Troop]] sub-[[:Category:Modes|mode]] of the Treasure Hunt game mode, the others being [[Sparky]] and the [[Archer Queen]].
** The Fisherman is 1 of 2 troops that has been featured in the [[Obstacle Course]] game mode, the other being Barbarians.
*The Fisherman is 1 of 23 cards that has had its [[Elixir]] cost changed, the others being Bomber, [[Fire Spirit]], Royal Recruits, [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], Musketeer, [[Three Musketeers]], [[Heal]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], Skeleton Army, P.E.K.K.A., Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], Bowler, [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Rage]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Fisherman's name is Maurice as said by his fish in [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F4AmkFBJFTA The Flood trailer]; however, in the Japanese language setting of the game, his name is Triton.
**According to The Flood trailer, the Fisherman has a Scottish accent.
*The Fisherman's "Fish Slap" is likely a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fish-Slapping_Dance The Fish-Slapping Dance], a short comedy sketch performed on [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monty_Python%27s_Flying_Circus Monty Python's Flying Circus] in 1972. 
**Occasionally when attacking, the Fisherman exclaims "''Fish Slap''".
***The Fisherman’s fish is voiced by Allen Enlow.
***The Fisherman is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Mega Minion]], Wizard, Hog Rider, P.E.K.K.A., [[Dark Prince]], Bowler, Ram Rider, Electro Wizard, [[Princess]], Ice Wizard, Magic Archer, [[Lumberjack]], [[Mother Witch]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Boss Bandit]], Archer Queen, [[Little Prince]], and the [[Terry]].
*The [[Card Mastery]] task "Get Over Here!" is a reference to a quote mentioned by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scorpion_(Mortal_Kombat) Scorpion] in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortal_Kombat Mortal Kombat].
*When a Fisherman is defeated, he drops his fish which flops on the ground for a while before it disappears. The other units that drop items upon death are the Knight, Rascal Boy, Mega Minion, Dark Prince, [[Executioner]], Mega Knight, Sparky, [[Super Knight]], Golden Knight, and the Little Prince.
*The Fisherman, Ram Rider, [[Phoenix]], and the Lumberjack are the only normal spawning {{Rarity|Legendary}} troops that do not fall from the sky when deployed.
*The Fisherman is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Fisherman is the subject of 3 [[Emotes]]. His fish is also the subject of 3 Emotes.
**The Fisherman is the subject of a [[King's Tower|Tower Skin]].
**The Fisherman is the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
*When 2 Fishermen face each other, only 1 of the 2 Fishermen will be able to hook the other one, slowing him down afterwards. This results in 1 of the 2 winning the duel instead of both being defeated at the same time.
*The Fisherman was originally going to appear in late 2017, with a hook and trap mechanic. However, the hook and trap mechanic [https://www.reddit.com/r/ClashRoyale/comments/atmpr5/official_what_weve_been_up_to_this_week_feb_22/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=web2x&context=3 were dropped], which lead to the creation of the Hunter. Ultimately, the Fisherman was added in one of Clash Royale's updates.

